### Parkings API Tests
### Complete CRUD operations testing

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@token = your-jwt-token-here

### 1. Login to get JWT token (replace with actual credentials)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "password"
}

### 2. Create a new parking (minimal data)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "parkingCode": "PARK001",
  "parkingName": "Central Business Parking",
  "regionId": 1
}

### 3. Get all parkings (should show the created parking)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Get the specific parking by ID (replace {id} with actual ID from step 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Update the parking with detailed information
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shortcode": "CBP",
  "latitude": 51.5074,
  "longitude": -0.1278,
  "street": "123 Business Avenue",
  "postalCode": "SW1A 1AA",
  "town": "Business District",
  "managerName": "John Smith",
  "managerPhone": "+44 20 7946 0958",
  "managerEmail": "john.smith@parking.com",
  "emergencyContact": "Emergency Line: +44 20 7946 0999",
  "parkingSpaces": 150,
  "active": true
}

### 6. Get the updated parking details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Create another parking for testing
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "parkingCode": "PARK002",
  "parkingName": "North Side Parking Hub",
  "regionId": 1
}

### 8. Search parkings by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/search?query=central
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Get parkings by company
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/by-company/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Get parkings by country
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/by-country/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Get parkings by region
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/by-region/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Check if parking exists
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/1/exists
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Assign parking to another region (if you have region ID 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/1/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "regionId": 2,
  "parkingCode": "PARK001-R2",
  "metadata": {
    "assignment_reason": "Expansion to cover multiple regions",
    "priority": "High"
  }
}

### 14. Check if parking is assigned to region
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/1/regions/2/exists
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Remove parking from region
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/1/regions/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Try to create parking with duplicate code (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "parkingCode": "PARK001",
  "parkingName": "Another Central Parking",
  "regionId": 1
}

### 17. Update parking with invalid data (should fail validation)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "latitude": 200,
  "longitude": 400,
  "managerEmail": "invalid-email",
  "parkingSpaces": -10
}

### 18. Delete the second parking
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19. Verify deleted parking is not in the list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 20. Try to get deleted parking by ID (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Additional Test Cases

### 21. Create parking with maximum field lengths
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "parkingCode": "PARK003",
  "parkingName": "Extended Name Parking Facility with Very Long Name",
  "regionId": 1
}

### 22. Update with boundary coordinate values
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "latitude": 90.0,
  "longitude": 180.0,
  "parkingSpaces": 1
}

### 23. Test empty search query (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/search?query=
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 24. Test search with special characters
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/search?query=parking&
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 25. Get non-existent parking (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 26. Update non-existent parking (should return 404)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "parkingName": "Updated Name"
}

### 27. Delete non-existent parking (should return 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 28. Test assigning parking to non-existent region (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/parkings/1/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "regionId": 99999
}

### Expected Results Summary:
### 1. Create parking ? Success with ID 1
### 2. Get all ? Shows created parking
### 3. Get by ID ? Returns detailed parking info
### 4. Update ? Success with updated fields and computed latLong
### 5. Search ? Returns matching parkings
### 6. Filter endpoints ? Return appropriate subsets
### 7. Region assignment ? Success with mapping created
### 8. Duplicate code ? 400 Bad Request error
### 9. Invalid validation ? 400 Bad Request with validation errors
### 10. Delete ? 204 No Content, parking soft-deleted
### 11. Coordinate computation ? latLong field automatically calculated
### 12. Manager email validation ? Enforced on update
### 13. Company inheritance ? Automatic from region selection